s10-5-p24 : Block
s10-5-p24 = prose (cons "The displayed relation deliberately retains \(H,T,S\); an actual migration may change the state representation or snapshot only with a *separate* simulation relating the old and new observations and preserving the issued effects. A response to an outstanding request must be delivered to the new continuation under the **same request token**, and cannot trigger a second issue of that request. A state at an arbitrary machine instruction is not a safe swap point unless its source-continuation relation has been constructed. Turn and response boundaries are useful examples, not universal privileged cut points." nil)
